.TH IMPROV-IMPORT-CSV 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-import\-csv \- Import a CSV or TSV file into a new input measure
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov import\-csv\fR [OPTIONS] <db> <file.csv> <measure\-id> <measure\-name> <value\-col> <dim\-col:cat\-id:cat\-name>...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a CSV or TSV file into a new input measure.
.PP
Columns are header names, or 0\-based indices with \-\-no\-header. The delimiter is a comma unless \-\-tsv is given or the file ends in .tsv. Example: improv import\-csv m.db sales.csv 100 Revenue r t:1:Time p:2:Product
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-tsv\fR
Tab\-separated
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-header\fR
The file has no header row: columns are 0\-based indices
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fIfile.csv\fR>
The file to read
.TP
<\fImeasure\-id\fR>
The new measure\*(Aqs numeric id
.TP
<\fImeasure\-name\fR>
The new measure\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fIvalue\-col\fR>
The column holding the values
.TP
<\fIdim\-col:cat\-id:cat\-name\fR>
COLUMN:CATEGORY\-ID:CATEGORY\-NAME: a column, and the category its distinct values become items of
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-files (5).
